    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0481" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/337</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-11T14:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 11, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11:15 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>
                    Sir Edward Grey informs me that Japan
                    finds herself unable to refrain from war with Germany, The German Ambassador at
                        <pb facs="0482" n="168" xml:id="pg168"/> Tokyo has made further refraining
                    impossible. Japan assures Britain that she is anxious to respect both the
                    neutrality and the integrity of China. The Anglo-Japanese treaty binds both
                    parties to it to respect her integrity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
